    "definitions": [],
    "lead_paragraphs": [
      "We propose 6 starred restaurants in Barcelona. Haven’t you heard yet that it is possible to enjoy the haute cuisine of Barcelona’s great restaurants and still make ends meet? As we all know, tasting the elaborations of Michelin stars is usually a great plan, but also a very expensive plan (even if it is good value for money). Solution: opt for its midday formula. A more economical proposal with the same distinctive quality. In these 6 Michelin-starred restaurants in Barcelona you can eat for less than 50€ with more than assured success. Treat your palate to a gastronomic experience while taking care of your pocket. It is important to reserve a table! If you are into gastronomic experiences you can find more at Gastroshows .",
      "Caelis is the restaurant of the Ohla Barcelona hotel . The French chef Romain Fornell , at the helm, proposes a Catalan cuisine with Gallic roots based on seasonal products accompanied by different pairings. A culinary experience for the diner due to, among other factors, its flavors and its open kitchen.",
      "From Wednesday to Saturday from 13:30h to 15:30h , they offer the ‘Caelis Menu’ for 42 euros (VAT included) . It consists of: a starter (to choose between two), a main course (to choose between two) followed by a selection of cheeses or a sweet dessert , plus a coffee or tea . The menu also includes one of two wines (either white or red) suggested by the sommelier. Not valid for groups of more than 12 people."
    ],
